.TH TASKMANAGER 1 "2026-10-30" "taskmanager 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taskmanager \- Windows 7, 8 and 10 style Task Manager for Linux, macOS and BSD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskmanager
[\fB\-\-win7\fR | \fB\-\-win8\fR | \fB\-\-win10\fR | \fB\-\-layout\fR \fILAYOUT\fR]
[\fB\-\-tux\fR | \fB\-\-no\-tux\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taskmanager
shows running applications, processes, services, startup programs, users
and live performance graphs, laid out like the Task Manager of Windows 7,
Windows 8 or Windows 10.
.PP
.I Tux mode
keeps the chosen layout and adds the information only Linux provides:
kernel process states, systemd units, cgroups, OOM scores, USS/PSS memory,
pressure stall information, sensors, CPU vulnerabilities and more, plus a
dedicated
.I Tux
tab.
.PP
The layout and Tux mode can also be changed at run time from the
.I View
menu. Both choices are remembered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-win7 ", " \-\-win8 ", " \-\-win10
Start with the Windows 7, Windows 8 or Windows 10 layout.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " LAYOUT"
Same as above, with
.I LAYOUT
being one of
.BR win7 ", " win8 " or " win10 .
.TP
.B \-\-tux
Turn Tux mode on.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tux
Turn Tux mode off.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TASKMANAGER_QT
Force the Qt binding:
.B pyside6
or
.BR pyqt6 .
By default PySide6 is used when installed, otherwise PyQt6.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/TaskManager/TaskManager.conf
Settings (layout, Tux mode, columns, window sizes).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/taskmanager/app_history.json
Resource usage collected for the App history tab.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR top (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR proc (5)
